(text "DRONECAN BLOCK (Rev 14.0) - analysis/can_phy_analysis.py -> analysis/can_phy_report.json\n- U7 TCAN334G (G = 5 Mbit/s CAN FD grade). STB pin 8 has an integrated pull-DOWN (DS pin table):\n  normal mode during MCU reset (PD3 Hi-Z) and after init (hwdef PD3 OUTPUT LOW); GPIO 70 high = standby.\n  SHDN pin 5 tied to GND. TXD pull-up keeps the bus recessive while PD1 is Hi-Z.\n- Termination 2 x 60.4R + 4.7 nF to GND (120.8R, 119.6..122.0R worst case, ISO 11898-2 100..130R).\n  JP1/JP2 bridged: this node is a bus end. Cut BOTH for a mid-bus FC (keeps C46 off the bus).\n- D4 PESD2CANFD24V-T: ESD/transient only (VBR >= 25.5 V > U7 abs-max 14 V) - J3 must never see VBAT.\n- FD data rate: legal CAN_P1_FDBITRATE 1/2/4/5 Mbit/s; 8 is ILLEGAL (TCAN334G 5 Mbit/s, TDC SSP on edge).\n- J3 pin 1 +5V comes from the power sheet: current-limit to <= 1 A (GH contact rating).\nLAYOUT RULES\n- J3 -> D4 -> JP/R45/R46/C46 -> U7 in that order on one layer, CANH/CANL as a coupled symmetric pair,\n  equal length (+/-0.5 mm), no vias between D4 and J3, <= 25 mm total (lumped, no 120R impedance control).\n- D4 pin 3 and C46 GND: own via each into In1 GND at the connector edge (short ESD return, no shared via).\n- C44 within 1 mm of U7 pin 3; U7 >= 5 mm from ESC phase nodes; no CAN pair under or beside motor pads.\n" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 609.6 93.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "97dd3102-66e1-55e1-accf-90f999a4f178"))
